  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Grid moves addressed by cell rather than by name, which is what an authoritative drag and drop needs.\nA client that dragged an item could previously only say which item it meant, and a client naming its\nown item is one that can name an item it does not have.\n\n### Added\n\n- `GridContainerModel.PlacementAt`: what occupies one cell, or null when it is empty or off the grid.\n- `GridContainerModel.TryPlaceAt(GridPlacement, ...)`: exact placement of an already-described\n  footprint. Identity is re-read from the instance store and plain stacks are bounded by the catalog,\n  so a placement handed in by a client cannot rename an instance or mint an oversized stack.\n- `GridContainerModel.TryMoveTo`: moves whatever occupies a source cell to an exact destination, across\n  two grids or within one, turning it a quarter on the way when asked. The caller names cells and never\n  an item, which is the property that makes it safe to drive from a drag. Both grids are restored when\n  the destination refuses, so a rejected move cannot leave an item owned by neither.",
